  "note": "Triennial election of Londonderry Corporation (all twenty members: five aldermen and fifteen councillors), due Wednesday 21 May 1958: no contest. Twelve Unionists and eight Nationalists (Anti-Partitionists in the Derry Journal) were nominated for the twenty seats and returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6; Derry Journal, 9 May 1958, p. 1). New members: T. H. Buchanan (North, in place of Councillor E. J. Oxford), Seamus Deeney, Cornelius Glackin and Charles McDaid jun. (South); Councillors John P. Harvey and James Hegarty became aldermen in place of Aldermen E. G. McAteer and M. Coyle, who did not seek renomination. Colhoun was the Mayor. Returned unopposed."
